  (uuid_generate_v4(), 'roger-skeet-jr-navajo-native-american-turquoise-sterling-silver-fan-pin-925-vint', '4611969165', 'https://www.etsy.com/listing/4611969165/roger-skeet-jr-navajo-native-american?click_key=EugH2sedQ8DY96Hl5Iy7rAo3RF6b%3ALTcfbbc946ab4110c217e2f9bacf882f6e71730c5c&click_sum=b90a686f&ls=a&ga_order=most_relevant&ga_search_type=all&ga_view_type=gallery&ga_search_query=Navajo+jewelry&ref=search_grid-293398-17-6&sr_prefetch=1&pf_from=search&frs=1&sts=1',
   'Roger Skeet Jr Navajo Native American Turquoise Sterling Silver Fan Pin 925 Vintage Indian Southwest Western RS Chiseled Modernist', 'Vintage Roger Skeet Jr. Navajo Sterling and Turquoise Fan Pin Description: This signed Roger Skeet Jr. Navajo pin is a beautifully designed piece, a sterling silver fan whose scalloped rays spread out from an oval turquoise cabochon set high in a crisp sawtooth bezel. Deep chiseled lines radiate from the stone to divide the fan into broad, gently rounded rays, and each ray ends in its own scallop along the edge, so the outline follows the pattern of the lines. One side sweeps up into a longer rounded point, giving the fan an asymmetrical, wing-like shape. The turquoise is a strong blue-green with dark brown to black matrix scattered across the surface in an irregular web, which stands out sharply against the bright polished silver. The clean chiseled lines show off one of the techniques Skeet is documented for, used here in a modern, sculptural design. Roger Skeet Jr. is a Navajo silversmith, born around 1933, who began apprenticing with his father, Roger Skeet Sr., at the age of eight. When the Navajo Guild in Window Rock required a hallmark around 1955, he began stamping his work R.S. and RS. Father and son made silver bracelet frames for trader C. G. Wallace that Zuni artists inlaid with turquoise, and Roger Jr. is documented for stampwork, chisel work, repousse, set stones, concho belts, and sandcast pieces. Signed RS and marked Sterling on the reverse. Measurements and Specifications: Weight: 4.4 grams Material: Sterling Silver, Turquoise Main Stone: Turquoise Stone Color: Blue-Green Stone Characteristics: Dark brown to black matrix in an irregular web Stone Shape: Oval Cabochon Number of Gemstones: 1 Setting Type: Sawtooth Bezel Stone Measurements: 0.47 in L x 0.34 in W (11.9 mm x 8.6 mm) Overall Measurements: 1.46 in L x 0.90 in W (37.1 mm x 22.9 mm) Pin Clasp: C-Clasp Design: Asymmetrical scalloped fan with radiating chiseled rays and raised turquoise Technique: Hand chiseling, Sawtooth bezel setting, Hand-cut scalloped edge Artist: Roger Skeet Jr. Signed/Un', 'turquoise-jewelry',
